Input: {"question": "What is Thomas Rich's military rank?", "original_source_segments": {"D1S1": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 0, "end": 15, "text": "**Thomas Rich**"}, "D1S2": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 17, "end": 202, "text": "Thomas Rich (1733-1803) was a British politician and naval officer who served as a Member of Parliament (MP) and held the senior rank of Admiral in the Royal Navy of the United Kingdom."}, "D1S3": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 203, "end": 228, "text": "**Early Life and Career**"}, "D1S4": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 230, "end": 292, "text": "Thomas Rich was born in 1733 to a prominent family in England."}, "D1S5": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 293, "end": 420, "text": "Little is known about his early life, but he began his naval career at a young age, rising through the ranks of the Royal Navy."}, "D1S6": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 421, "end": 437, "text": "**Naval Career**"}, "D1S7": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 439, "end": 575, "text": "Rich's naval career spanned several decades, during which he served with distinction and earned promotions to increasingly senior ranks."}, "D1S8": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 576, "end": 734, "text": "According to the Oxford Dictionary of National Biography, Rich was promoted to Rear-Admiral of the Blue in 1794, and later to Vice-Admiral of the Red in 1799."}, "D1S9": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 735, "end": 847, "text": "[1] This progression of ranks demonstrates his growing expertise and leadership abilities within the Royal Navy."}, "D1S10": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 848, "end": 864, "text": "**Admiral Rank**"}, "D1S11": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 866, "end": 977, "text": "The most significant evidence of Rich's admiral rank comes from his appointment as Admiral of the Blue in 1801."}, "D1S12": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 978, "end": 1142, "text": "[2] This senior rank is one of the highest in the Royal Navy, and Rich's achievement of it is a testament to his dedication and service to the British naval forces."}, "D1S13": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1143, "end": 1167, "text": "**Parliamentary Career**"}, "D1S14": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1169, "end": 1301, "text": "In addition to his naval career, Rich also served as a Member of Parliament (MP) for the constituency of Sandwich from 1784 to 1790."}, "D1S15": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1302, "end": 1445, "text": "[3] This dual role demonstrates his commitment to public service and his ability to balance the demands of both military and political careers."}, "D1S16": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1446, "end": 1460, "text": "**References**"}, "D1S17": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1462, "end": 1565, "text": "[1] Oxford Dictionary of National Biography, \"Rich, Thomas (1733-1803)\" (Oxford University Press, 2004)"}, "D1S18": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1567, "end": 1595, "text": "[2] The London Gazette, \"No."}, "D1S19": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1596, "end": 1622, "text": "15415\" (February 14, 1801)"}, "D1S20": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1624, "end": 1725, "text": "[3] History of Parliament Online, \"RICH, Thomas (1733-1803)\" (Institute of Historical Research, 2019)"}, "D1S21": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1727, "end": 1850, "text": "This Wikipedia entry presents comprehensive evidence for the statement that Thomas Rich holds the military rank of Admiral."}, "D2S1": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 0, "end": 11, "text": "Thomas Rich"}, "D2S2": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 13, "end": 149, "text": "Thomas Rich (1733-1803) was a British Member of Parliament and a distinguished military officer who held the rank of Chief of Artillery."}, "D2S3": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 150, "end": 174, "text": "Early Life and Education"}, "D2S4": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 176, "end": 267, "text": "Thomas Rich was born on February 12, 1733, in London, England, to a family of modest means."}, "D2S5": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 268, "end": 382, "text": "He received his early education at Eton College, where he demonstrated a keen interest in mathematics and science."}, "D2S6": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 383, "end": 505, "text": "Rich's academic prowess earned him a scholarship to Christ Church, Oxford, where he studied military tactics and strategy."}, "D2S7": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 506, "end": 521, "text": "Military Career"}, "D2S8": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 523, "end": 641, "text": "Rich's military career began in 1755, when he enlisted as a lieutenant in the British Army's Royal Artillery Regiment."}, "D2S9": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 642, "end": 727, "text": "He saw action in the Seven Years' War, participating in the Battle of Quebec in 1759."}, "D2S10": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 728, "end": 856, "text": "Rich's bravery and tactical acumen during the battle caught the attention of his superiors, who promoted him to captain in 1762."}, "D2S11": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 857, "end": 985, "text": "In 1775, Rich was appointed as the Chief of Artillery for the British Expeditionary Force during the American Revolutionary War."}, "D2S12": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 986, "end": 1105, "text": "He played a crucial role in the Battle of Bunker Hill, where his artillery tactics helped to repel the American forces."}, "D2S13": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1106, "end": 1210, "text": "Rich's leadership and expertise earned him the respect of his peers and the admiration of his superiors."}, "D2S14": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1211, "end": 1231, "text": "Parliamentary Career"}, "D2S15": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1233, "end": 1305, "text": "In 1784, Rich retired from active military service and entered politics."}, "D2S16": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1306, "end": 1419, "text": "He was elected as a Member of Parliament for the constituency of Windsor, a seat he held until his death in 1803."}, "D2S17": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1420, "end": 1517, "text": "During his parliamentary career, Rich was a vocal advocate for military reform and modernization."}, "D2S18": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1518, "end": 1653, "text": "He chaired several committees on military affairs and was instrumental in shaping British military policy during the late 18th century."}, "D2S19": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1654, "end": 1676, "text": "Studies and References"}, "D2S20": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1678, "end": 1781, "text": "* \"The Artillery Tactics of Thomas Rich\" by Major General John Smith, Journal of Military History, Vol."}, "D2S21": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1782, "end": 1789, "text": "12, No."}, "D2S22": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1790, "end": 1798, "text": "3 (1995)"}, "D2S23": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1799, "end": 1843, "text": "* \"Thomas Rich: A Biographical Study\" by Dr."}, "D2S24": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1844, "end": 1889, "text": "Emily Johnson, Oxford University Press (2001)"}, "D2S25": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1890, "end": 1951, "text": "* \"The British Army in the American Revolutionary War\" by Dr."}, "D2S26": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1952, "end": 1982, "text": "James Wilson, Routledge (2010)"}, "D2S27": {"docu